Changes in this edition
-----------------------
  Date: 2026-11-14

  1. Knowledge catalog expanded from 66 topics / 117 KB to 85 topics / 275 KB,
     adding: faction goals, rules, templates and initiative; power balance (BOP);
     collections; loops and array operations; event targets; scripted GUI
     super-events and window framework; version migration (1.13 / 1.15 / 1.16.9
     -> 1.17.3); define overriding; special projects; equipment modules and
     designs; building slots and construction; character traits; ideas and
     modifier reference; OOB and start-of-game setup; bookmark scenario
     selection; reversed AI strategy; AI areas and AI templates.
     Bodies are English; tags carry Chinese synonyms so Chinese queries match.

  2. New MCP tool `register_hoi4_gfx_sprites`: scans an existing image directory
     inside a mod workspace, reads every `interface/**/*.gfx` first, and appends
     only the missing `spriteType` registrations to a `.gfx` file. Idempotent by
     texture path, reports already-registered sprites, orphaned registrations
     whose texture file is gone, and skipped name collisions. Ships with unit and
     end-to-end tests.

  3. `build.rs`: the Windows icon/version resource is now optional. When no
     resource compiler is available (`llvm-rc`, a Windows SDK `rc.exe`, or `RC`),
     the build prints a warning and links no resource instead of panicking, so the
     project compiles with a plain Rust toolchain on any platform. A compiler that
     is found but fails is still a hard error.

  4. Documentation: `docs/features.*` (en, zh-CN, ja, ru) document the new tool
     and the knowledge catalog; CONTRIBUTING.md explains the optional resource
     compiler; README and localized READMEs carry the modified-edition notice.

